AB  - This study introduces an innovative data-BIM integrated digital twin framework for the quality monitoring residential developments. The framework amalgamates residential building information modeling (RBIM), surveying sensors and Internet of Things (SSIoT) technologies to establish a multi-faceted and multi-scale monitoring system. Within this framework, RBIM serves as a residential information twin model that aggregates comprehensive life cycle data of residential projects, encompassing design, building, operation, and maintenance. The physical things are linked to cyberspace via SSIoT technology, significantly improving data exchange and processing capabilities. To address the limitations of singular monitoring technology, a BIM collaborative multi-source data monitoring method for residential engineering quality is proposed, utilizing the BIM model alongside the advancement of real-time transmitting monitoring LiDAR, automated monitoring robots, GNSS, and various other sensors. This framework seeks to create a novel paradigm for intelligent, comprehensive data management and synthesizing heterogeneous data from several sources, focusing on the quality monitoring of residential projects to guarantee quality, safety, and operational efficiency.
