TI  - Joint detection PCD-based method for automatic construction of geometric digital twin in cable dome structure
T2  - ENGINEERING STRUCTURES
LA  - English
KW  - Geometric digital twin
KW  - Cable dome structure
KW  - Object detection
KW  - Geometric topological reconstruction
KW  - Joint deviation
AB  - The geometric digitization of cable dome structures using Point Cloud Datasets (PCD) holds significant importance as it serves as a foundational step in constructing the Digital Twin of such structures. However, accurately detecting the positions of structural joints for effective construction of a geometric digital twin from PCD remains a challenging task. To address this issue, we propose an enhanced algorithm and system solution for joint detection based on target recognition. The method leverages a novel shape estimation model to identify structural components by randomly sampling the minimum set of points from the point cloud. Subsequently, connection joints and their coordinates are determined according to the spatial relationships of the components. This enables the digital reconstruction of the structure based on the topological relationships of the joints, ultimately facilitating the establishment of a geometric digital twin. The efficacy and reliability of the proposed method are validated through a case study involving PCD from a scaled cable dome structure, demonstrating outstanding performance in joint detection and fitting with accuracy levels exceeding 99 %. Based on the results of joint detection, the feasibility of model topology reconstruction is corroborated, and the potential for accurately assessing joint deviations is explored. These research findings serve to advance the progress of digital twins in large-span dome structures, facilitating enhanced analysis and inference regarding structural performance, safety, and stability within the digital twin framework.
