AB  - In the process of large-span steel structure construction, because its structure has not yet formed a complete system, so its mechanical properties and safety status are not stable, and it is necessary to control the safety of the structure, and the current traditional structural health monitoring (SHM) has the problems of high cost, easy to be interfered, and unpredictable, etc. The digital twin, as a popular technology in the engineering industry, has the characteristics of multidimensionality, high integrative, intelligent and real-time, so it is very necessary to introduce digital twin technology in the construction process. In this paper, a digital twin-driven intelligent safety control method for large-span steel structures is proposed. The digital twin model is constructed by collecting actual engineering data and integrating finite element analysis data. Based on the random forest algorithm, The influencing factors of the overall jacking construction process of the large-span steel mesh frame are analyzed to obtain the importance ranking of the features affecting the process. The results show that the most influential features for the overall jacking construction are the height difference of the jacking frame and the jacking speed. Therefore, the above two should be paid special attention to in the construction safety control.
