KW  - Infrared point cloud fusion
KW  - Structural anomaly detection
KW  - Digital twin mapping
KW  - THERMOGRAPHY
KW  - IMAGES
AB  - As the service life of some buildings increases, some safety hazards may seriously endanger public safety and cause economic losses. Defect detection and management are necessary steps to eliminate potential safety hazards. At present, the inspection of building exterior walls mostly relies on manual inspection, which is highly subjective, risky and has low inspection accuracy. To this end, this study developed an algorithm based on the infrared and point cloud data fusion model of the Point Cloud Reconstruction Network (PCRNet) to increase the depth information of the model and improve its understanding of complex scenes. For the anomaly detection of regular and irregular geometric envelope structures, an automatic anomaly detection algorithm model of geometric envelope structures based on convolutional neural network (CNN) is proposed. By comparing the extracted temperature information with the labeled data in the real abnormal data set, the detection accuracy, recall rate and accuracy of the evaluation model have been improved. Finally, a reverse digital twin mapping method based on the abnormal information of spatial geometric envelope structure of infrared point clouds is proposed, which is convenient for systematic and object-oriented management. The experimental results show that among 299 experimental data points, single-data anomaly detection can be completed quickly. The average accuracy rate of various hazard detection is 92%, the Precision is 96.3 %, the Recall Rate is 94%, the F1-Score is 95.1 %, and the average detection speed is 5.21 s. It only takes 26 min to complete the building anomaly detection.
